{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxzRZraQ3EvZRSESxANn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ran the judge stage on `catalogue-title` and the verdict is **pass**. The verdict is in `.dca-factory/runs/catalogue-title/judge.md`. I didn't run the gate on it: the stage rules call for a gate only after the test, build and tidy stages.\n\nThis story is an adoption (`status: adopted`): the shop already titles the catalogue page, so nothing was built and the story's diff is empty. In that mode the only question is whether the existing test proves the scenario, so I didn't do the usual design and code-quality reviews.\n\n- **The test does prove it:** `CatalogTitleE2ETest` opens `/products` in a real browser and checks that the page title is exactly \"Product Catalog\".\n- **It would catch a regression:** if the catalogue page stopped setting its title, the page layout would fall back to \"domaincentric.commerce\" and the test would fail.\n- **The \"seeded catalogue\" setup isn't missing:** the test runs against the shop with its seed data, and the title doesn't depend on what's in the catalogue anyway.\n\nThere are no defects. I noted one overlap that I didn't count against the story: the title is also checked under another criterion, `catalogue-page-heading` from story CAT-01. Whoever owns the spec should decide whether both keys should stay.\n\nThe prompt named only the judge stage, so I wrote no `document.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":842,"cache_read_input_tokens":43347,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":842},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"294c7f0b-b8a0-4e13-b1d0-25291ebde5c5","uuid":"350249f8-5e